{"name":"Open Book","hex":"#f5f1e5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"open book","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something whose salient aspects are obvious or easily interpreted.","A person who responds candidly to questions or openly displays their emotions or intentions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open_book"}],"entries":[{"title":"An Open Book (poetry collection)","blocks":[{"text":"An Open Book (2004) is a collection of poems by Orson Scott Card."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/OSCanopenbook.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An_Open_Book_(poetry_collection)","wikidata":"Q4750186"},{"title":"Open access","blocks":[{"text":"Open access (OA) is a set of principles and a range of practices through which nominally copyrightable publications are delivered to readers free of access charges or other barriers. With open access strictly defined, or libre open access, barriers to copying or reuse are also reduced or removed by applying an open license for copyright, which regulates post-publication uses of the work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Open_Access_logo_PLoS_transparent.svg/330px-Open_Access_logo_PLoS_transparent.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_access","wikidata":"Q232932"},{"title":"Open Book (Fatherson album)","blocks":[{"text":"Open Book is the second studio album from Scottish alternative rock band Fatherson and was released on 3 June 2016. The album includes the singles \"Always\", \"Lost Little Boys\" and \"Just Past the Point of Breaking\". The album marks the band's first release with their new label Easy Life/Sony Music UK."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Open_Book_Fatherson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_Book_(Fatherson_album)","wikidata":"Q25096936"},{"title":"Book","blocks":[{"text":"A book is a written work of substantial length created by one or more authors. The work is typically printed on many sheets of paper as pages bound together into a bookblock, then glued to the middle of a foldable cover that protects the pages. Before the wide adoption of the modern printing press, codices were used to create handwritten manuscripts. Older writing media include scrolls and clay tablets. Nowadays, books can be distributed in other forms like audiobooks, and electronic books (ebooks). Books are broadly classified into fiction, which contains invented or imaginary narratives; and non-fiction, which contains content intended as factual truth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Gutenberg_Bible%2C_Lenox_Copy%2C_New_York_Public_Library%2C_2009._Pic_01.jpg/330px-Gutenberg_Bible%2C_Lenox_Copy%2C_New_York_Public_Library%2C_2009._Pic_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book","wikidata":"Q571"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/DOAJ_growth.png/500px-DOAJ_growth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/DOAJ_growth.png/1280px-DOAJ_growth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/DOAJ_growth.png/500px-DOAJ_growth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADOAJ_growth.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/PMC_growth.png/500px-PMC_growth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t